> f(x: real) = x where x > 5
> domain f
domain of f:
  x: real (default [-10, 10])
  where x > 5
  no conditions: total on its parameter types
  defined on (numerically, grid of 20001 over [-10, 10]):
    x in [5.001, 10]
> range f
range of f:
  [5.001, 10]   min at x ≈ 5.001, max at x ≈ 10
  grid of 20001 points over [-10, 10] (default; give x a range), extrema refined at critical points
> g(x: u8) = 1 << x where x < 4
> domain g
domain of g:
  x: u8, 0..255
  where x < 4
  requires 0 <= x < 8  (shift amount; C UB otherwise)
  defined at 4 of 4 points
  over all 4 points of the domain
> range g
range of g -> u8:
  1..8   (4 distinct values)
  values: 1..2, 4, 8
  fits in u4
  over all 4 points of the domain
